{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mqiznf3kk2j","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/zonoid","title":"schedule wakeup killed PID liveness cache","summary":"For ScheduleWakeup sleepers, `process.kill(pid, 0)` can still report a just-SIGTERM'd detached `node -e` sleeper as alive for a short teardown window. The scheduler records PIDs it has just killed and treats them as not alive for immediate dedup/cancel/sweep checks; this is scoped to the scheduler sleeper path, whose child has no SIGTERM handler and exits shortly after.","created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-06-18T04:17:01.232Z","vec":[-0.07546120136976242,0.049464453011751175,0.028613833710551262,0.015409830026328564,0.12230747193098068,-0.03661941736936569,-0.021241167560219765,-0.01712018810212612,0.0309218168258667,0.04833899810910225,-0.03473518416285515,0.02748251147568226,-0.05438968539237976,-0.009979549795389175,-0.03194050490856171,0.0030291597358882427,-0.01609848253428936,0.035511091351509094,0.010626273229718208,-0.004114341922104359,-0.01767060160636902,0.09014685451984406,0.06402658671140671,0.014672036282718182,0.017009606584906578,-0.04963536188006401,0.026412397623062134,-0.04814177006483078,0.03204746171832085,-0.004037284292280674,0.0381433479487896,0.0013164592674002051,-0.06823448091745377,-0.08036920428276062,0.0715315118432045,0.12423543632030487,0.0338250957429409,-0.0733097642660141,-0.07058249413967133,0.036271438002586365,0.16110268235206604,0.057559866458177567,-0.05863538011908531,-0.062851183116436,-0.03942043334245682,0.026638684794306755,-0.11612152308225632,-0.06375457346439362,-0.06227048113942146,-0.011641841381788254,-0.031374335289001465,-0.04006371274590492,-0.0012356635415926576,0.1028103306889534,0.003880606032907963,0.0727209597826004,0.03311814367771149,-0.0014530153712257743,0.042616695165634155,0.05231305584311485,-0.07221167534589767,0.04524955525994301,0.04657219350337982,-0.03297596424818039,0.07947535067796707,0.06917387992143631,-0.007656892761588097,-0.084514938294887